# Amdocs

>Amdocs Limited (NASDAQ: DOX) is a global provider of software products and managed services for communications, media, and financial-services companies. Founded in 1982 and headquartered in Saint Louis, Missouri, USA, Amdocs helps service providers run billing, customer experience, network, and AI/GenAI operations at scale, supporting more than 350 communications and media customers and 600+ content-creator relationships across 85+ countries.

Amdocs employs roughly 27,000 people worldwide and reported revenue of $4.53 billion in fiscal year 2025 (ended September 30, 2025). Its current flagship strategy centers on **aOS**, the "Agentic Operating System for Telco," which combines the **Cognitive Core** GenAI foundation (the evolution of the former amAIz suite) with **CES26** (formerly CES25), Amdocs' telco-native, agent-driven suite spanning business, operations, and network domains. The platform is open by design, supports multiple LLMs, and is delivered with partners including Microsoft, AWS, NVIDIA, and Google Cloud.

Leadership as of mid-2026: Shimie Hortig is President & CEO (succeeded Shuky Sheffer, effective March 31, 2026); Tal Rozenfeld is Chief Financial Officer (succeeded Tamar Rapaport-Dagim, effective June 1, 2026); Eli Gelman is Chairman of the Board; Anthony Goonetilleke is Group President of Technology & Head of Strategy. Recent corporate developments include the ~$200 million acquisition of MATRIXX Software (real-time charging/monetization, closed Q1 FY2026), an expanded multi-year AWS collaboration announced at MWC 2026, and renewed/extended agreements with T-Mobile, Vodafone Germany, AT&T, Globe, PLDT/Smart, and other Tier-1 operators.

